{"Title":"An Act relative to accommodations for special needs students taking the MCAS examination","BillNumber":"H430","DocketNumber":"HD1098","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BJA1","Name":"Bruce J. Ayers","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BJA1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T10:58:36.313"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BJA1","Name":"Bruce J. Ayers","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BJA1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T10:58:36.3133333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H430/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Ayers of Quincy, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 430) of Bruce J. Ayers relative to accommodations for special needs students taking the Massachusetts Comprehensive Assessment System (MCAS) examination.  Education.","DocumentText":"\tThe fourth paragraph of section 1I of chapter 69 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2014 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting, after the word “needs”, in line 48, the following words:— \r\n\tand such children shall be afforded the same accommodation each uses or requires in the classroom throughout the year.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}